        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If a retired employee declined enrollment for himself/herself or dependents when first eligible and the retired employee's or dependent's other health care coverage was through continuation coverage from a previous employer (coverage mandated by the Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985, or COBRA), the retired employee or dependent must exhaust his or her COBRA coverage to be eligible for the special enrollment period.",
